From: Isaac Connor <connortechnology@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] vf_drawtext_ni: mark the per-frame options as runtime
 parameters

Against Quadra V5.8.0 (libxcoder 5806tCr2).

Every option in ni_drawtext_options[] carries plain FLAGS. Upstream
vf_drawtext.c defines

  #define TFLAGS FLAGS|AV_OPT_FLAG_RUNTIME_PARAM

and tags text, fontcolor, fontsize, x, y and the rest of the per-frame
set with it.

Since FFmpeg 7.0, av_opt_set() and the generic process_command() refuse
an option that lacks AV_OPT_FLAG_RUNTIME_PARAM once the object is
initialised. So on 7.x every attempt to change the text after setup --
including the filter's own "reinit" command, which re-parses an option
string -- fails with

  Option 'text' is not a runtime option
  ... EINVAL

and the text set at graph construction is the only text the filter will
ever draw. There is no error at the draw itself: the filter keeps
running and keeps drawing the initial string.

Tag the options a caller changes per frame -- the 32 text, foreground
colour, font size, x, y and font slots, and their unindexed slot-0
aliases -- matching the set upstream marks.

--- a/libavfilter/vf_drawtext_ni.c
+++ b/libavfilter/vf_drawtext_ni.c
@@ -294,6 +294,12 @@
 
 #define OFFSET(x) offsetof(NetIntDrawTextContext, x)
 #define FLAGS AV_OPT_FLAG_FILTERING_PARAM|AV_OPT_FLAG_VIDEO_PARAM
+/* Options a caller may change on an initialised filter, as upstream
+ * vf_drawtext.c marks them. Since FFmpeg 7.0 av_opt_set() and
+ * process_command() refuse an option without this flag on an
+ * initialised object, so without it every "reinit" command fails
+ * with EINVAL and the text can never be changed after setup. */
+#define TFLAGS FLAGS|AV_OPT_FLAG_RUNTIME_PARAM
 
 static const AVOption ni_drawtext_options[] = {
     { "fontfile",    "set font file",        OFFSET(fontfile[0]),           AV_OPT_TYPE_STRING, {.str=NULL},  0, 0, FLAGS },
